IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rra-types`
IMPORT `rra-tenancy`
IMPORT `rra-bidding`

-- Renters' Rights Act 2025 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Renting case` HAS
    `the tenancy`                                       IS A `Tenancy terms`
    `a rent period`                                     IS A MAYBE `Rent period`
    `a letting`                                         IS A MAYBE `Letting conduct`

DECLARE `Renting position` HAS
    `runs as a periodic tenancy`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `rent periods permitted`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `advance-rent term of no effect`                    IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `rent due on`                                       IS A MAYBE DATE
    `rental bidding penalty may be imposed`             IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `maximum rental bidding penalty`                    IS A NUMBER

@ref HA 1988 ss 4A, 4B; ss 56-57
@export default The position under the Renters' Rights Act 2025 (UK) for an assured tenancy in England: whether fixed-term or period terms are of no effect so that it runs as a periodic tenancy (HA 1988 s 4A(1)), whether its rent periods are permitted (s 4A(3)); for a rent period, whether the term for rent due in advance is of no effect and the day the rent is due (s 4B); and for a letting, whether a rental bidding penalty may be imposed (ss 56-57, maximum £7,000). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Renting case`  @desc The tenancy terms, any rent period, and any letting conduct
GIVETH A `Renting position`
`the renting position for` c MEANS
    `Renting position` WITH
        `runs as a periodic tenancy`                    IS
            t's `an assured tenancy`
        `rent periods permitted`                        IS `the rent periods are permitted in` t
        `advance-rent term of no effect`                IS
            CONSIDER c's `a rent period`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST r  THEN JUST (`the term for rent due in advance is of no effect for` t `in` r)
        `rent due on`                                   IS
            CONSIDER c's `a rent period`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST r  THEN JUST (`the day the rent is due for` t `in` r)
        `rental bidding penalty may be imposed`         IS
            CONSIDER c's `a letting`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST l  THEN JUST (`a rental bidding penalty may be imposed for` l)
        `maximum rental bidding penalty`                IS `the maximum rental bidding penalty`
    WHERE
        t MEANS c's `the tenancy`
